## 1. Running

```powershell
.\mvnw.cmd -q test-compile
.\mvnw.cmd test "-Dtestcase.ids=TC_01_Login"
.\mvnw.cmd test "-Dtestcase.ids=TC_00_DATA,TC_01_ENTS"
.\mvnw.cmd test "-Dtestcase.ids=TC_03" "-Denvironment=QA"
```

| Switch | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `-Dtestcase.ids=A,B` | Runs exactly these test cases, ignoring the Execution flag |
| `-Denvironment=QA` | Overrides the Environment column for every selected row |
| `-Dexecution.control.writeback=false` | Does not write PASS / FAIL back into ExecutionControl.xlsx |
| `-Dbrowser=CHROME -Dbrowser.force=true` | Uses this browser whatever the Browser column says |
| `-Ddb.bootstrap=false` | BISS test cases use the herd / username from TestData.xlsx instead of the database |

The runner finds `<TestCase_ID>.feature` anywhere under `src/test/resources/Test_Cases/` (any sub-folder depth).
Every test case also needs a row in TestData.xlsx (the Password column is used by every login).

**Recommended order:** run `TC_00_DATA` first in a run. It fills the Test Data Vault for every selected test case,
so the test cases do not wait for slow queries.

