## 4. Runtime test data

No herd number or login needs to be typed in a feature file. Values are taken from Oracle at run time.

### 4.1 Tokens in feature files

| Token | Value |
|---|---|
| `{transferor.herd}` `{transferor.name}` `{transferor.address}` | transferor of the current transfer pair |
| `{transferee.herd}` `{transferee.name}` `{transferee.address}` | transferee of the current pair |
| `{agent}` `{transferor.login}` `{transferee.agent}` `{transferee.login}` | who creates / who accepts |
| `{auto.agent}` `{auto.agent.2}` ... | the agent with the most usable herds, the second best, ... |
| `{etf.code}` `{etf.partner}` | ETF picked by TC_14_ENTS and the login of its partner |
| `{random}` | TC_14_ENTS: pick a random ETF from the dropdown |

A plain value still works, so a herd can be pinned for debugging.

### 4.2 Test Data Vault

`runtime-data/vault` (git-ignored, it holds farmer names and herds - never commit it).

- `TC_00_DATA` reads which test cases are selected, works out how many herds each needs, runs the pool queries in
  parallel and stores the rows. It refills after the weekly database refresh (`data.refresh.day`) and spot-checks
  rows that are already there (agent link still current, application not started, login still mapped).
- Every herd handed out is RESERVED, then USED (passed) or BAD (failed, with the reason). A herd is not handed out twice.
- `data.force.refresh=true` refills everything once (set it back to false afterwards).

| Pool | Used by |
|---|---|
| `ENTS_AGENT`, `ENTS_ETF`, `ENTS_NO_ENTS`, `ENTS_INDIVIDUAL`, `ENTS_YOUNG_FARMER` | ENTS test cases |
| `BISS_NOT_STARTED`, `BISS_IND_CISYF`, `BISS_PARTNERSHIP` | TC_03 family and other BISS agent test cases |

### 4.3 Checking a query

Every query lives in `DBRouter` under a label. The SQL files in `guide/sql/` are the same queries with the
parameters filled in, ready for SQL Developer (CENTEST_BISS_DATA, CENTEST_BISS_INET, CENTEST_ENTS_DATA).

